# WebUI testing

- Runner: **Vitest** + **Testing Library** (`@testing-library/react`, `user-event`). Tests live under `webui/src/tests/` (follow existing files).
- Assert **user-visible behavior**: roles, labels, text, and `data-testid` only when roles/labels are insufficient.
- Prefer `screen.getByRole` / `findByRole` over brittle CSS class or DOM structure queries.
- Mock network/gateway at the API/client boundary; do not assert private component internals or implementation details.
- Wrap interactions that update state with Testing Library patterns (`userEvent`, `await findBy…`); avoid manual `act` unless necessary.
- Keep tests focused; add coverage when changing behavior users can observe (routing, settings save, empty states, errors).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
expect(container.querySelector(".rounded-full")?.textContent).toBe("Save");

// ✅ GOOD
expect(screen.getByRole("button", { name: /save/i })).toBeEnabled();
await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: /save/i }));
expect(await screen.findByText(/up to date/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
```

Run: `cd webui && npm test` (or `npm test -- --run path/to/file.test.tsx`).
